{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgM8yjko7rapgph3cE1hd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GX4wTMcPLrPQzU17A9koBX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md'\nt=open(p).read()\ni=t.index('## Readiness gaps')\nm=re.compile(r'```json\\n(.*?)\\n```',re.S).search(t,i)\ng=json.loads(m.group(1))\ng=[x for x in g if x['id']!='jvm-language-family-classfile']\nby={x['id']:x for x in g}\nby['contract-forward-hints']['detail']+=\" D24: no new token/day; EVERY question reworded into a spec (sha256 'ZIP central-directory order (1-based)', format rule list, full HCFG layout + per-container carrier rule) -- Day 26 + neko_bytecode still open; D24 Scala's `Foo$` module vs forwarder Main-Class is a plausible meaning of 'primary classfile named by that unit'.\"\nby['theme-facts-recording']['detail']+=\" d24: changed method `score(Ljava/lang/String;)I` only (class `Day24<Role>000$`), vulnerable nonEmpty-then-charAt(0) (null -> NullPointerException, CWE-476) vs corrected Option(s).filter(nonEmpty).map(charAt 0).getOrElse(-1), $-class sizes 4660 vs 5628, main identical (host-model lookupswitch decoy 32 / success 49 / failure 27 / default failure 1, then score(\\\"benign\\\") + decodeConfig().length), trace scala_patch_diff_trace / benign_control_and_reversion_only + control_positive.\"\nby['member-basename-vocabulary']['detail']+=\" D24 timed modes re-shaped domain (`<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid`), mutex (`Global\\\\Huntress<12 uppercase hex>`) and url (`https://<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid/<word>/<10hex>`) too; role tokens `vulnerable`/`corrected` follow `sample-`.\"\nby['build-pair-router']['detail']+=\" D24 SEEN as a vulnerable/corrected twin (Scala jars) -- the generic qualifier peel covered it with zero code.\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"jvm-method-patch-diff-facts\",\"concept\":\"Backfill of the D24 theme on the d24 twin jars (and any future JVM twin): per-class/per-method bytecode diff of vulnerable vs corrected -- changed method name + descriptor, what changed, before/after facts\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Fixtures: the cached D24 jars (challenges/day24/binary-spot-the-difference/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d24--sample-{vulnerable,corrected}.jar; only `score(Ljava/lang/String;)I` in `Day24<Role>000$` differs). lib.binary.jvm_patch_diff(jar_a, jar_b) -> match classes after stripping the role token from class names (Day24Vulnerable000$ ~ Day24Corrected000$), match methods by name+descriptor, compare Code attributes with constant-pool operands RESOLVED to symbolic names (raw CP indexes shift between builds), ignore LineNumberTable/StackMapTable. Expose: changed_methods (JSON list of `name(descriptor)` or `name`), changed_class, unchanged_methods, method_count per member, code_length/instruction_count before/after, added/removed invoke targets (e.g. +scala/Option$.apply, +scala/Option.filter/map/getOrElse, -scala/collection/StringOps$.nonEmpty$extension), added invokedynamic lambdas (`$anonfun$score$N`), classfile sizes, fix_kind token (null_guard/bounds_check/length_check/exception_handler/constant_change). Labels unknown: prefer javap spellings (`score`, `(Ljava/lang/String;)I`) and read the question's rule text.\"},\n {\"id\":\"vulnerability-trigger-proof\",\"concept\":\"'Prove the old one was really broken': derive the triggering input for the changed function and each build's outcome statically (exception/fault vs safe return)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"JVM: a tiny bytecode evaluator for leaf methods (aload/iconst/ifeq/ifnull/invoke of a stub model: java.lang.String length/charAt/isEmpty/equals/hashCode, scala Predef.augmentString (identity), StringOps.nonEmpty$extension/isEmpty, Option.apply/filter/map/getOrElse, BoxesRunTime) evaluated over a candidate set derived from the diff's guards (null, \\\"\\\", single char, index==length, -1, Integer.MIN/MAX); first input where the builds differ = trigger. Outcomes: `java.lang.NullPointerException` / `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException` / `StringIndexOutOfBoundsException` vs the corrected return (D24: null -> NPE vs -1). Native: unicorn-emulate the function with the trigger argument (map a stack, stub libc), report fault type/address. Never execute the sample itself. Facts: trigger_input, vulnerable_outcome, corrected_result, exception_class.\"},\n {\"id\":\"native-function-patch-diff\",\"concept\":\"Patch diff for native twin pairs (ELF/PE, C/C++/Rust/Go): which function changed and how (inserted bounds check, replaced unsafe call, changed constant/comparison)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Likeliest sequel to D24 (the lane alternates languages; a C/C++ twin is the classic patch-diff). lib.binary.native_patch_diff(a, b): match functions by symbol, else by (call targets, referenced strings/imports, size, CFG shape); normalise capstone instructions (mask RIP-relative/absolute addresses and call targets, keep immediates) and hash per function; emit changed_functions (symbol names in address order), per-function added/removed instructions, inserted `cmp`+`ja/jae/jb/jbe` pairs (bounds check), replaced imports (strcpy->strncpy, gets->fgets, sprintf->snprintf, memcpy length change), changed frame size (`sub rsp, N`), comparison flips (`jl`->`jb` signedness, `jle`->`jl` off-by-one), added `test reg,reg; je` (null check). Fixtures: gcc -O0/-O2 vuln/fixed pairs for off-by-one, missing bounds check, strcpy overflow, signedness, format string, null-after-free; one stripped pair. Tools present: capstone, rz-diff (`rz-diff -t functions a b`), objdump.\"},\n {\"id\":\"vulnerability-class-classifier\",\"concept\":\"Name the bug class a fix addresses as a CWE token + snake_case name (null deref 476, OOB read 125 / write 787, off-by-one 193, int overflow 190, signedness 195, format string 134, UAF 416, double free 415, div-by-zero 369, unchecked return 252, TOCTOU 367, command injection 78, SQLi 89, path traversal 22, unsafe deserialization 502)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Rule table over the diff facts of jvm-method-patch-diff-facts / native-function-patch-diff / managed-patch-diff-dotnet: added null guard / Option wrap / ifnull / `test;je` -> CWE-476; added index/length compare before array/charAt/memcpy -> 125/787; `<=`->`<` -> 193; `add`->`add.ovf`/Math.addExact/`__builtin_add_overflow` -> 190; `jl`->`jb` -> 195; printf(user)->printf(\\\"%s\\\",user) -> 134; free+null or use-after-free removal -> 416; divisor check -> 369; Runtime.exec/system/ProcessBuilder argument sanitising -> 78; ObjectInputStream.readObject filter -> 502; path normalise/`..` check -> 22. D24 fixture = CWE-476. Emit `CWE-476` and `null_pointer_dereference`; GM spelling unknown -> watch for an enum with accepted_values and read the question rules.\"},\n {\"id\":\"scala-module-class-facts\",\"concept\":\"Scala (and other JVM-language) identity facts for the d24 group backfill and the D26 'primary classfile named by that unit' rule: forwarder vs `$` module class, ScalaSignature/ScalaSig, TASTy, lambdas\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D24 jars: `Day24<Role>000.class` = static forwarder (Main-Class, 1.2 KB) + `Day24<Role>000$.class` = module (MODULE$, encodedConfig, decodeConfig, score, main). Expose per member: main_class, primary_class (the class holding the logic / HCFG ldc = the `$` module), forwarder_class, has_scala_signature (RuntimeVisibleAnnotations `Lscala/reflect/ScalaSignature;` or `ScalaSig` attribute), scala_major (2 vs 3: `.tasty` entries / `TASTY` attribute), source_file (`Day24Vulnerable000.scala`), method lists + method_count of BOTH classes (incl <init>/<clinit>, table order), access_flags decimal, classfile major/minor, invokedynamic bootstrap count, `$anonfun$` synthetic methods. Also route 'primary classfile named by that unit' when the question names a class (take it verbatim) or a source unit (`X.scala` -> the class whose SourceFile matches and holds main/logic). Clojure (`<ns>__init.class`) / Groovy (`$getStaticMetaClass`) shapes as synthetic fixtures.\"},\n {\"id\":\"managed-patch-diff-dotnet\",\"concept\":\".NET twin assemblies (vulnerable/corrected dll): IL method-body diff by type+method+signature with token resolution\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Same contract as jvm-method-patch-diff-facts for pe_cli twins: dnfile MethodDef RVA -> IL bytes, decode with the prebuilt IL call-site decoder, resolve tokens to `Type::Method` / string literals, ignore metadata-token renumbering and MVID/timestamp; report changed_methods (`Namespace.Type::Method`), added `ldnull/brfalse`/`?.` null guards, `ldlen` bounds compares, `add.ovf` checked arithmetic, try/catch regions (exception clauses diff). Fixtures: D22/D23 cached dlls as single-build controls; build twins only if `dotnet build` works offline, else hand-patch IL bytes of a copy (same length) for a synthetic pair.\"},\n {\"id\":\"stripped-twin-function-matching\",\"concept\":\"Match functions between two STRIPPED native builds to find the patched one (no symbols): BinDiff/Diaphora-style heuristics\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D15 shipped a stripped/symbolized pair; a stripped vulnerable/corrected pair is a natural escalation. Recover function starts (prologues, call targets, .eh_frame FDEs -- pyelftools CFI gives exact ranges even when stripped), then match by: referenced strings/imports, callee/caller sets, size, BB count, normalised-instruction hash, constant set; unmatched or hash-different = changed. Report the changed function's file offset/VA, its .eh_frame range and, if the symbolized twin exists in another group/member, its name. Fixtures: gcc pairs `strip -s`, -O2.\"},\n {\"id\":\"crash-exploitability-facts\",\"concept\":\"Native 'prove it is broken' facts: stack buffer size, distance from buffer to saved RIP/canary, overflow length that faults, faulting instruction, mitigations (canary/NX/PIE/RELRO)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"From capstone over the vulnerable function: frame size (`sub rsp, N`), buffer offset (`lea rdi, [rbp-0xNN]` passed to gets/strcpy/read/memcpy/scanf %s), canary load `mov rax, fs:0x28` + `__stack_chk_fail`, read length argument; distance_to_return = NN + 8 (rbp) ; first faulting length via unicorn emulation with a cyclic (de Bruijn) pattern; checksec-style facts from program headers (GNU_STACK flags, GNU_RELRO + BIND_NOW, ET_DYN+INTERP). Corrected twin: same facts showing the bound. Fixtures: gcc -fno-stack-protector / -fstack-protector-strong pairs.\"},\n {\"id\":\"binary-patch-file-apply\",\"concept\":\"Binary patch FILES as group members applied to a base member: bsdiff (`BSDIFF40`, bz2 blocks), IPS (`PATCH` ... `EOF`), BPS/UPS (`BPS1`/`UPS1` + crc32), xdelta3/VCDIFF (`d6 c3 c4 00`), unified diff text\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Two builds, one fix' could next ship base + patch instead of two builds. Pure-Python appliers (no bsdiff4/xdelta3 binaries assumed): bsdiff40 (header 32 B: ctrl/diff lengths + new size, three bz2 streams), IPS records (u24 offset, u16 size, RLE when size 0), BPS (varint actions + source/target/patch crc32), VCDIFF RFC 3284 (no secondary compressor). Facts: patch_format, target_size, target_sha256, changed byte ranges / count, patched function (map offsets through the section table), crc checks valid. Fixtures: generate with Python writers for each format over a small ELF.\"},\n {\"id\":\"symbolic-input-solver\",\"concept\":\"Find an input that reaches a target (vulnerable path, accept branch, decoy vs success) with angr/z3 when hand-evaluation is impractical: crackme/license checks, multi-step guards\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"angr (venv) blank_state at the function with symbolic args/stdin, avoid-list = failure branches, find = target address (crash site, success string xref, `return 1`); z3 directly for JVM/IL guard chains extracted by the bytecode evaluators (hashCode lookupswitch -> string preimage among the binary's own literals first). Hard caps: 60 s, 4 GB; output the concrete input as hex + printable. Fixtures: gcc serial-check (per-char xor/add compare), a hash-gated branch, and the D24 host-model lookupswitch (preimages analysis/workstation/sandbox).\"}\n]\ng=new+g\nassert len({x['id'] for x in g})==len(g)\nbody=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)+\"\\n]\"\nt=t[:m.start(1)]+body+t[m.end(1):]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not (st.get('binary-reverse-engineering:'+x['id'],{}).get('ok') or st.get('binary-reverse-engineering:'+x['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(g),'pending',len(pend),pend)\nEOF\npython3 -c \"\nimport json,re;t=open('reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md').read();sec=t[t.index('## Readiness gaps'):]\ng=json.loads(re.search(r'\\`\\`\\`json\\n(.*?)\\n\\`\\`\\`',sec,re.S).group(1));print('valid',len(g),set(k for x in g for k in x))\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2227,"cache_read_input_tokens":142983,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2227},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64843a9b-06dd-4b22-a704-45f90784829c","uuid":"02e755e6-479e-46c0-a2e2-3f3db382c9f5","timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:27:15.980Z","request_id":"req_011CgM8yjUvxC1feE2arUiUe","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GX4wTMcPLrPQzU17A9koBX":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md'\nt=open(p).read()\ni=t.index('## Readiness gaps')\nm=re.compile(r'```json\\n(.*?)\\n```',re.S).search(t,i)\ng=json.loads(m.group(1))\ng=[x for x in g if x['id']!='jvm-language-family-classfile']\nby={x['id']:x for x in g}\nby['contract-forward-hints']['detail']+=\" D24: no new token/day; EVERY question reworded into a spec (sha256 'ZIP central-directory order (1-based)', format rule list, full HCFG layout + per-container carrier rule) -- Day 26 + neko_bytecode still open; D24 Scala's `Foo$` module vs forwarder Main-Class is a plausible meaning of 'primary classfile named by that unit'.\"\nby['theme-facts-recording']['detail']+=\" d24: changed method `score(Ljava/lang/String;)I` only (class `Day24<Role>000$`), vulnerable nonEmpty-then-charAt(0) (null -> NullPointerException, CWE-476) vs corrected Option(s).filter(nonEmpty).map(charAt 0).getOrElse(-1), $-class sizes 4660 vs 5628, main identical (host-model lookupswitch decoy 32 / success 49 / failure 27 / default failure 1, then score(\\\"benign\\\") + decodeConfig().length), trace scala_patch_diff_trace / benign_control_and_reversion_only + control_positive.\"\nby['member-basename-vocabulary']['detail']+=\" D24 timed modes re-shaped domain (`<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid`), mutex (`Global\\\\Huntress<12 uppercase hex>`) and url (`https://<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid/<word>/<10hex>`) too; role tokens `vulnerable`/`corrected` follow `sample-`.\"\nby['build-pair-router']['detail']+=\" D24 SEEN as a vulnerable/corrected twin (Scala jars) -- the generic qualifier peel covered it with zero code.\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"jvm-method-patch-diff-facts\",\"concept\":\"Backfill of the D24 theme on the d24 twin jars (and any future JVM twin): per-class/per-method bytecode diff of vulnerable vs corrected -- changed method name + descriptor, what changed, before/after facts\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Fixtures: the cached D24 jars (challenges/day24/binary-spot-the-difference/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d24--sample-{vulnerable,corrected}.jar; only `score(Ljava/lang/String;)I` in `Day24<Role>000$` differs). lib.binary.jvm_patch_diff(jar_a, jar_b) -> match classes after stripping the role token from class names (Day24Vulnerable000$ ~ Day24Corrected000$), match methods by name+descriptor, compare Code attributes with constant-pool operands RESOLVED to symbolic names (raw CP indexes shift between builds), ignore LineNumberTable/StackMapTable. Expose: changed_methods (JSON list of `name(descriptor)` or `name`), changed_class, unchanged_methods, method_count per member, code_length/instruction_count before/after, added/removed invoke targets (e.g. +scala/Option$.apply, +scala/Option.filter/map/getOrElse, -scala/collection/StringOps$.nonEmpty$extension), added invokedynamic lambdas (`$anonfun$score$N`), classfile sizes, fix_kind token (null_guard/bounds_check/length_check/exception_handler/constant_change). Labels unknown: prefer javap spellings (`score`, `(Ljava/lang/String;)I`) and read the question's rule text.\"},\n {\"id\":\"vulnerability-trigger-proof\",\"concept\":\"'Prove the old one was really broken': derive the triggering input for the changed function and each build's outcome statically (exception/fault vs safe return)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"JVM: a tiny bytecode evaluator for leaf methods (aload/iconst/ifeq/ifnull/invoke of a stub model: java.lang.String length/charAt/isEmpty/equals/hashCode, scala Predef.augmentString (identity), StringOps.nonEmpty$extension/isEmpty, Option.apply/filter/map/getOrElse, BoxesRunTime) evaluated over a candidate set derived from the diff's guards (null, \\\"\\\", single char, index==length, -1, Integer.MIN/MAX); first input where the builds differ = trigger. Outcomes: `java.lang.NullPointerException` / `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException` / `StringIndexOutOfBoundsException` vs the corrected return (D24: null -> NPE vs -1). Native: unicorn-emulate the function with the trigger argument (map a stack, stub libc), report fault type/address. Never execute the sample itself. Facts: trigger_input, vulnerable_outcome, corrected_result, exception_class.\"},\n {\"id\":\"native-function-patch-diff\",\"concept\":\"Patch diff for native twin pairs (ELF/PE, C/C++/Rust/Go): which function changed and how (inserted bounds check, replaced unsafe call, changed constant/comparison)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Likeliest sequel to D24 (the lane alternates languages; a C/C++ twin is the classic patch-diff). lib.binary.native_patch_diff(a, b): match functions by symbol, else by (call targets, referenced strings/imports, size, CFG shape); normalise capstone instructions (mask RIP-relative/absolute addresses and call targets, keep immediates) and hash per function; emit changed_functions (symbol names in address order), per-function added/removed instructions, inserted `cmp`+`ja/jae/jb/jbe` pairs (bounds check), replaced imports (strcpy->strncpy, gets->fgets, sprintf->snprintf, memcpy length change), changed frame size (`sub rsp, N`), comparison flips (`jl`->`jb` signedness, `jle`->`jl` off-by-one), added `test reg,reg; je` (null check). Fixtures: gcc -O0/-O2 vuln/fixed pairs for off-by-one, missing bounds check, strcpy overflow, signedness, format string, null-after-free; one stripped pair. Tools present: capstone, rz-diff (`rz-diff -t functions a b`), objdump.\"},\n {\"id\":\"vulnerability-class-classifier\",\"concept\":\"Name the bug class a fix addresses as a CWE token + snake_case name (null deref 476, OOB read 125 / write 787, off-by-one 193, int overflow 190, signedness 195, format string 134, UAF 416, double free 415, div-by-zero 369, unchecked return 252, TOCTOU 367, command injection 78, SQLi 89, path traversal 22, unsafe deserialization 502)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Rule table over the diff facts of jvm-method-patch-diff-facts / native-function-patch-diff / managed-patch-diff-dotnet: added null guard / Option wrap / ifnull / `test;je` -> CWE-476; added index/length compare before array/charAt/memcpy -> 125/787; `<=`->`<` -> 193; `add`->`add.ovf`/Math.addExact/`__builtin_add_overflow` -> 190; `jl`->`jb` -> 195; printf(user)->printf(\\\"%s\\\",user) -> 134; free+null or use-after-free removal -> 416; divisor check -> 369; Runtime.exec/system/ProcessBuilder argument sanitising -> 78; ObjectInputStream.readObject filter -> 502; path normalise/`..` check -> 22. D24 fixture = CWE-476. Emit `CWE-476` and `null_pointer_dereference`; GM spelling unknown -> watch for an enum with accepted_values and read the question rules.\"},\n {\"id\":\"scala-module-class-facts\",\"concept\":\"Scala (and other JVM-language) identity facts for the d24 group backfill and the D26 'primary classfile named by that unit' rule: forwarder vs `$` module class, ScalaSignature/ScalaSig, TASTy, lambdas\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D24 jars: `Day24<Role>000.class` = static forwarder (Main-Class, 1.2 KB) + `Day24<Role>000$.class` = module (MODULE$, encodedConfig, decodeConfig, score, main). Expose per member: main_class, primary_class (the class holding the logic / HCFG ldc = the `$` module), forwarder_class, has_scala_signature (RuntimeVisibleAnnotations `Lscala/reflect/ScalaSignature;` or `ScalaSig` attribute), scala_major (2 vs 3: `.tasty` entries / `TASTY` attribute), source_file (`Day24Vulnerable000.scala`), method lists + method_count of BOTH classes (incl <init>/<clinit>, table order), access_flags decimal, classfile major/minor, invokedynamic bootstrap count, `$anonfun$` synthetic methods. Also route 'primary classfile named by that unit' when the question names a class (take it verbatim) or a source unit (`X.scala` -> the class whose SourceFile matches and holds main/logic). Clojure (`<ns>__init.class`) / Groovy (`$getStaticMetaClass`) shapes as synthetic fixtures.\"},\n {\"id\":\"managed-patch-diff-dotnet\",\"concept\":\".NET twin assemblies (vulnerable/corrected dll): IL method-body diff by type+method+signature with token resolution\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Same contract as jvm-method-patch-diff-facts for pe_cli twins: dnfile MethodDef RVA -> IL bytes, decode with the prebuilt IL call-site decoder, resolve tokens to `Type::Method` / string literals, ignore metadata-token renumbering and MVID/timestamp; report changed_methods (`Namespace.Type::Method`), added `ldnull/brfalse`/`?.` null guards, `ldlen` bounds compares, `add.ovf` checked arithmetic, try/catch regions (exception clauses diff). Fixtures: D22/D23 cached dlls as single-build controls; build twins only if `dotnet build` works offline, else hand-patch IL bytes of a copy (same length) for a synthetic pair.\"},\n {\"id\":\"stripped-twin-function-matching\",\"concept\":\"Match functions between two STRIPPED native builds to find the patched one (no symbols): BinDiff/Diaphora-style heuristics\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D15 shipped a stripped/symbolized pair; a stripped vulnerable/corrected pair is a natural escalation. Recover function starts (prologues, call targets, .eh_frame FDEs -- pyelftools CFI gives exact ranges even when stripped), then match by: referenced strings/imports, callee/caller sets, size, BB count, normalised-instruction hash, constant set; unmatched or hash-different = changed. Report the changed function's file offset/VA, its .eh_frame range and, if the symbolized twin exists in another group/member, its name. Fixtures: gcc pairs `strip -s`, -O2.\"},\n {\"id\":\"crash-exploitability-facts\",\"concept\":\"Native 'prove it is broken' facts: stack buffer size, distance from buffer to saved RIP/canary, overflow length that faults, faulting instruction, mitigations (canary/NX/PIE/RELRO)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"From capstone over the vulnerable function: frame size (`sub rsp, N`), buffer offset (`lea rdi, [rbp-0xNN]` passed to gets/strcpy/read/memcpy/scanf %s), canary load `mov rax, fs:0x28` + `__stack_chk_fail`, read length argument; distance_to_return = NN + 8 (rbp) ; first faulting length via unicorn emulation with a cyclic (de Bruijn) pattern; checksec-style facts from program headers (GNU_STACK flags, GNU_RELRO + BIND_NOW, ET_DYN+INTERP). Corrected twin: same facts showing the bound. Fixtures: gcc -fno-stack-protector / -fstack-protector-strong pairs.\"},\n {\"id\":\"binary-patch-file-apply\",\"concept\":\"Binary patch FILES as group members applied to a base member: bsdiff (`BSDIFF40`, bz2 blocks), IPS (`PATCH` ... `EOF`), BPS/UPS (`BPS1`/`UPS1` + crc32), xdelta3/VCDIFF (`d6 c3 c4 00`), unified diff text\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Two builds, one fix' could next ship base + patch instead of two builds. Pure-Python appliers (no bsdiff4/xdelta3 binaries assumed): bsdiff40 (header 32 B: ctrl/diff lengths + new size, three bz2 streams), IPS records (u24 offset, u16 size, RLE when size 0), BPS (varint actions + source/target/patch crc32), VCDIFF RFC 3284 (no secondary compressor). Facts: patch_format, target_size, target_sha256, changed byte ranges / count, patched function (map offsets through the section table), crc checks valid. Fixtures: generate with Python writers for each format over a small ELF.\"},\n {\"id\":\"symbolic-input-solver\",\"concept\":\"Find an input that reaches a target (vulnerable path, accept branch, decoy vs success) with angr/z3 when hand-evaluation is impractical: crackme/license checks, multi-step guards\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"angr (venv) blank_state at the function with symbolic args/stdin, avoid-list = failure branches, find = target address (crash site, success string xref, `return 1`); z3 directly for JVM/IL guard chains extracted by the bytecode evaluators (hashCode lookupswitch -> string preimage among the binary's own literals first). Hard caps: 60 s, 4 GB; output the concrete input as